  "description": "<p>The University of Alabama, Birmingham, was established in 1969. It is a public research University offering 140 programs in 12 academic divisions and is known for internationally recognized research.</p><p>The student body is diverse, with approximately 1,084 international students from more than 110 countries enrolled at the University annually.</p><h2>What is the University of Alabama at Birmingham acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The University of Alabama at Birmingham acceptance rate is 81%.</p> <p>The University of Alabama, Birmingham's facilities are comprehensive and cover a range of amenities. The Mervyn H. Sterne Library is one of the largest academic libraries in Alabama, so students are empowered with a range of books, resources and multimedia materials. The Campus Recreation Center enables students to exercise using the weight rooms, cardio equipment, indoor track, basketball courts and more.</p><p>The UAB Hospital is a world-renowned medical facility offering patient care, research, and teaching services. Many students are attracted to its size as it is one of the largest academic medical centers in the United States. The UAB Comprehensive Cancer Center is a world-class research and treatment facility dedicated to fighting cancer through research, education, and patient care.</p><p>The Edge of Chaos is a collaborative space on campus that brings together researchers, innovators, and entrepreneurs to develop innovative solutions. The Alys Stephens Performing Arts Center is a state-of-the-art facility that hosts various performing arts events, including concerts and plays. The Bartow Arena is the University's indoor sports arena, used for basketball and volleyball games and other events. Regions Field is home to the Birmingham Barons, a minor league baseball team; a baseball stadium situated near campus.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus Green is an ample space where students can relax or study together. It partially gets its name from the 4,400+ trees surrounding the area. In the warmer weather, students gather for outdoor events. Students are significantly involved in student organizations on campus, with over 380 student clubs to choose from to find your tribe. The campus has won awards for championing diversity, and there are many traditions to have fun with, from the international festival to blazer splash and beyond. The city of Birmingham, USA, is nearby too.</p>",
