      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Alabama, Birmingham, was established in 1969. It is a public research University offering 140 programs in 12 academic divisions and is known for internationally recognized research.</p><p>The student body is diverse, with approximately 1,084 international students from more than 110 countries enrolled at the University annually.</p><p>The UAB Hospital is a world-renowned medical facility offering patient care, research, and teaching services. Many students are attracted to its size as it is one of the largest academic medical centers in the United States. The UAB Comprehensive Cancer Center is a world-class research and treatment facility dedicated to fighting cancer through research, education, and patient care.</p>",
